  "title": "A chord over a different bass note",
  "summary": "C/E means a C chord with E in the bass.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Slash chord",
      "body": "A chord symbol with a slash names the lowest note: **C/E** means a C chord with E at the bottom. This is a **slash chord**. The part before the slash is the chord; the part after is the note your left hand plays.\n\n**Why it matters:** Slash chords make bass lines walk smoothly: C, C/B, Am, Am/G steps down one note at a time. Band charts are full of them.",
